  "raw_text": "136\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy51\n):\n \nRut witin ra (Jehova) uba latwan kaikan\n \n–\n \nRuth really loved him\n \n/ Rut realmente lo amaba)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh11\n):\n \nlatwan wan kaiki ba mita,\n \n…\n \n–\n \nbecause of loving us,\n \n…\n \n/ por amarnos, ...)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh42\n):\n \nPana pana latwan tara kaiki kan kaia sa!\n \n–\n \nIt must be that they were loving each other greatly!\n \n/ ¡Debe ser que se\namaban mucho!)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nNaha tasba na yawan latwan kaikbiara\n \n–\n \nWe are not to love this world\n \n/ No debemos amar este mundo)\n\nLatwan ai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love me\n \n/ amarme\n\nLatwan mai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love you\n \n/ amarte\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nLatwan mai kaikisna\n \n–\n \nI love you\n \n/ te quiero\n)\n\nLatwan wan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love us\n \n/ amarnos\n\nLatwankira\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nlovely, precious, loving, loved, beloved, dear\n \n/ encantador, precioso, amoroso, amado, querido\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nwan uplika latwankira\n \n–\n \nour loved ones\n \n/ nuestros seres queridos\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(salutation at the beginning of a letter\n/\n \nsaludo al comienzo de una\n \ncarta\n):\n \nMuihni bara lakri latwankira nani\n \n–\n \nbeloved\n\nbrothers and sisters\n \n/ amados hermanos y hermanas\n)\n\nLaitwankira\n \n(construct)\n \n–\n \nmy beloved, my dear\n \n/ mi amado, mi querido\n\nLamtwankira\n \n(construct)\n \n–\n \nyour beloved, your dear\n \n/ tu amado, tu querido\n\nLamtwanka\n \n(construct)\n \n–\n \nyour beloved, your love, your mate\n \n/ tu amado, tu amor, tu compañero\n\nLatwan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nlove\n \n/ amor\n\n(Construct:\n \nLaitwanka lâka\n;\n \nLamtwanka lâka\n;\n \nLatwanka lâka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nBîlam nani bara daukankam nani ba wal pana pana lamtwanka lâka ba mariks\n \n–\n \nWith your words and deeds,\nshow each other your love\n \n/ Con tus palabras y acciones, muéstrense amor)\n\nLatwan lâka kasak\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntrue love, loyal love\n \n/ amor verdadero, amor leal\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-01/22\n):\n \nUpla kum ai pânika nani wal kasak sa, bara piua karna nani ra sin witin nani ra lulki swiras sa kaka,\nlatwan lâka kasak ba marikisa.\n \n–\n \nIf a person is true with their friends and doesn’t leave them in hard times (commitment),\n\nthey show loyal love.\n \n/ Si una persona es fiel con sus amigos y no los deja en los momentos difíciles (compromiso),\nmuestra amor leal.)\n\nLauaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nLawaia\n\nLaukaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nLawkaia\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nLauaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto cause to get angry, to infuriate\n \n/ hacer enojar, enfurecer\n\nLawaia\n \n(fs/ea:\n \nLauaia\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nLaukaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto get angry, to quarrel, to argue, to nag, to have jealousy, to be\njealous\n \n/ enojarse, pelear, discutir, regañar, tener celo, ser celoso\n\nLalawra\n \n(a/t:\n \nLalaura\n) (n\n-\nagent\n/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \none who gets angry easily, one who is quick to argue, one who gets\n\njealous\n \n/ uno que se enoja fácilmente, uno que es rápido para discutir, uno que se pone celoso\n\nNina t\nȃ\nwan lalawra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \none that does not tolerate any infidelity\n \n/ uno que no tolera\nninguna infidelidad\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Impakan Sturka 20:5\n):\n \nYang sika man Dawan G\nȃ\ndkam, nini t\nȃ\nwan lalawra sni\n \n–\n \nI am your Lord God, I\nam one that does not tolerate any infidelity\n \n/ Soy tu Señor Dios, soy uno que no tolera ninguna infidelidad)\n\nLawaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nanger\n \n/ ira\n\nLawi daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto discipline, to reprove, to exhort, to reprimand, to nag, to correct, to counsel\n \n/ disciplinar,\nreprobar, exhortar, reprender, regañar, corregir, aconsejar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-2 Timoti 3:16\n):\n \nUlbanka aiska...yamni sa...lawi daukaia\n \n–\n \nAll writing (scripture)...is good...to reprove\n \n/ Toda\nescritura...es buena...para reprobar)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Galesha 2:11\n):\n \nMawan kat lawi daukri\n \n–\n \nI reproved (him) to his face\n \n/ Lo reprendí a su cara)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-08/19\n):\n \nLawi ai daukisa taim wilinkira bîla walisna ki?\n \n–\n \nWhen I am counseled, do I willingly obey?\n \n/ Cuando\nme aconsejan, ¿obedezco voluntariamente?)\n\nLawi daukanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndiscipline, reproof, exhortation\n \n/ disciplina, reprensión, exhortación\n\nLawi dauk\ni wapni\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndiscipline, reproof, exhortation\n \n/ disciplina, reprensión, exhortación\n\nLa\nw\ni kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be angry\n \n/ estar enojado\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh80\n):\n \nSetan ba laui pali sa\n \n–\n \nSatan is very angry\n \n/ Satanás está muy enojado\n)\n\nLawanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nLauanka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nanger, rage, argument, nagging\n \n/ ira, discusión, regaños\n\n(Other construct forms /\n \nOtras formas constructivas:\n \nLawanki/Lauanki\n \n–\n \nmy anger\n \n/ mi enojo;\n \nLawankam/Lauankam\n \n–\n\nyour anger\n \n/ tu ira)\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \nLawanka\n \nis also the construct form of\n \nLawana\n \n/\n \nLawanka\n \nes también la\n \nforma constructiva de\n \nLawana\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nSofon\ní\nas\n \n2:3\n):\n \nDawan lawanka yua ra\n \n–\n \nin the day of (the) Lord’s anger\n \n/ en el día de (la) ira del Señor\n)\n\nLâwaia\n \n(Lawaia)\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nLâkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto dry, to wither, to become thin, to fade\n \n/ secarse, marchitarse, adelgazarse,\ndesvanecerse",
